WEBVTT

00:00:01.649 --> 00:00:03.649
It's got it in it.

00:00:03.649 --> 00:00:05.650
I got it.

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.650
It's a great to ease.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.650
There's got to be a panel starting.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:13.650
There's got it.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.650
Don't touch it.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:16.649
I got it!

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:53.990
Is it true that no one's ever read it before?

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:59.990
I read it in the internet that no one in the whole wide world knows about the warrior angel's secret battle cry is.

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:02.990
You've got to let me take a look at this.

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:03.990
You'll better look at this.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.989
You know better than that.

00:01:05.989 --> 00:01:09.989
Anybody opens that book, the value drops.

00:01:09.989 --> 00:01:10.989
I know.

00:01:10.989 --> 00:01:13.989
But aren't you at least curious what's inside?

00:01:13.989 --> 00:01:15.989
Of course.

00:01:15.989 --> 00:01:20.390
I mean, who wouldn't?

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:22.390
But if I so much as breathed at it funny,

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:27.469
my boss would kill me.

00:01:27.469 --> 00:01:31.469
Besides, there's nothing in that fantasy world

00:01:31.469 --> 00:01:34.469
that's gonna make a lick of difference out here in the real one, kid.

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:53.200
I'm sorry.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:02:02.810
Sorry.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:04.810
I can't see a thing in the helmet.

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.810
How is...

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.810
This is not what I had in mind

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.810
when Randall said I got to be embedded journalist for the day.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:12.810
Come on.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:16.810
It shouldn't be hard for Lois Lane to nail down a human interest piece here.

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.810
Save a hammer. Mama's gonna need a crowbar.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:19.810
I can't get anything out of these people.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.810
They keep looking at me like I'm from another planet.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.810
You're saying something.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:29.810
You know, no offense, but that armor doesn't exactly make you mis-approachable.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.810
Look.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:33.810
Don't be afraid.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:37.810
Right. No wonder Clark's been avoiding me.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:40.810
I am losing touch with fantasy without even realizing it.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:44.810
The last thing Clark feels when he thinks about you is boredom.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.810
Maybe I'm doing this to myself.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.810
You know, maybe it's a deep-rooted fear of intimacy.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:55.810
Maybe I'm not letting loose because every time I do, things fall apart.

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:56.810
Maybe my therapist was right.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:59.810
You know, she said I used to have these fantasies about Clark and now,

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.810
not so much as it's Jordan Limerick.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.810
No, maybe you just need to calm down.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.810
and focus on your work.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.810
Oh, sorry.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:15.599
You're right.

00:03:15.599 --> 00:03:19.599
And maybe you should take advantage of being immersed in your element.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.599
Get your hands off of the digital world

00:03:21.599 --> 00:03:24.599
and onto some hunky human fantasy for a change.

00:03:24.599 --> 00:03:26.599
Have a little fun. One of us should.

00:03:26.599 --> 00:03:31.610
All right.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.610
Good.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:35.610
Now, I have to go make a phone call.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.610
Promise me you're going to kick the crackberry to the curb.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:38.610
I promise.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:53.379
I can't move of doing this.

00:03:53.379 --> 00:04:07.949
Warrior Angels, really just the kid?

00:04:07.949 --> 00:05:48.060
Are you okay?

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:49.060
I'm sorry, I'm late.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:53.060
But, um, I guess I got caught up with some chores,

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:55.060
but I'm in the truck on the way there now.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:56.060
Oh, good.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:59.060
Can you grab something for my place while you're at it?

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.060
Check in the closet.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.060
Sure, like you said, I'm already late, so...

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:05.060
I'm cashing in a rain check.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.060
You can not renege on a rain check.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:09.060
Lois, can I rain check on your rain check?

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.060
No, you have been catching in so many rain checks lately

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.060
that I am soaking wet with disappointment.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:19.060
Luckily, I'm driving by the talon right now, Lois.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.060
What do you need?

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:23.060
What was that wishing sound?

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:26.060
Nothing. I just had the truck window open.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:28.060
Okay, this is what I got.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:30.060
Some red leather thing.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:31.060
Nope.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:36.939
Salute the flag?

00:06:36.939 --> 00:06:37.939
Nice Gavin, more grabbing.

00:06:37.939 --> 00:06:43.040
French meat outfit.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.040
Need to know basis.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:51.139
There's a garment bag.

00:06:51.139 --> 00:06:52.139
Finally.

00:06:52.139 --> 00:06:53.139
There you go. Now that wasn't so hard, was it?

00:06:53.139 --> 00:06:54.139
Wasn't so hard was it?

00:06:54.139 --> 00:06:55.139
Yeah, a piece of cake.

00:06:55.139 --> 00:06:56.139
You're my hero.

00:06:56.139 --> 00:07:18.329
You know, after that heroic hit and run,

00:07:18.329 --> 00:07:22.329
it would be hard for even the most distressed damsel, not to take offense.

00:07:22.329 --> 00:07:24.329
What would a hero say?

00:07:24.329 --> 00:07:29.399
You're welcome, citizen.

00:07:29.399 --> 00:07:37.779
And you left a not-so-s-s-suttle trail of breadcrumbs on your way over here for the quick change.

00:07:37.779 --> 00:07:39.779
I'm sorry.

00:07:39.779 --> 00:07:41.779
This is all kind of new to me.

00:07:41.779 --> 00:07:43.779
I didn't realize how fast I was.

00:07:43.779 --> 00:07:45.779
No sonic boom.

00:07:45.779 --> 00:07:49.779
It's not that fast, I guess.

00:07:49.779 --> 00:07:50.779
Did you want to...

00:07:50.779 --> 00:07:53.420
What?

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:57.100
Oh.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:07.240
Um, not very heroic.

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:11.259
Good street look, though.

00:08:11.259 --> 00:08:13.259
Uh-huh.

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:17.259
Look, whether you feel like it or not, I know a superhero when I see one.

00:08:17.259 --> 00:08:20.259
I'm sort of in the business of helping superheroes.

00:08:20.259 --> 00:08:23.259
I don't think anyone's dad talked about that on Career Day.

00:08:23.259 --> 00:08:26.759
Are you for real?

00:08:26.759 --> 00:08:28.759
Yeah, I'm about as real as it gets.

00:08:28.759 --> 00:08:30.759
Chloe Sullivan.

00:08:30.759 --> 00:08:32.759
Steven Swift.

00:08:32.759 --> 00:08:33.759
Ow!

00:08:33.759 --> 00:08:34.759
Sorry.

00:08:34.759 --> 00:08:41.759
You know, maybe we can talk about how you fit in among the world's finest over coffee sometime.

00:08:41.759 --> 00:08:45.759
That sounds pretty cool.

00:08:45.759 --> 00:08:57.610
So, did you want to get that coffee now or...

00:08:57.610 --> 00:09:01.500
No? Uh, yeah.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:02.500
Okay.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:04.500
I mean, if you're not doing anything.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.500
Yeah.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.740
Ladies first.

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:26.330
I get a frown that much when you've been sweating like a pot roast all after you.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.330
Sorry, Lois, I just don't get all this.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:29.330
The colors, the costumes.

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:33.330
It's like everyone has a popcorn image of what being a hero is all about.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:35.330
It's called a fantasy, Clark.

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:41.330
An escape, something, I don't know, more magical than what we have in our normal lives.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:49.330
The reality of being a hero, it's about sacrifice, responsibility, and accountability, from what I've heard.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:53.330
Did you and Chloe both just swear off whimsy?

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:55.330
Was there a memo?

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:58.330
Look, a costume isn't just about hiding who you are.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:03.330
It's about seeing the world in a way that you haven't before.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:08.179
What's your dream?

00:10:08.179 --> 00:10:11.179
Getting swept away in a little fantasy might do you some good every once in a while.

00:10:11.179 --> 00:10:15.580
Ladies got a point.

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:19.580
Without a dash of fantasy, life's just life.

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:21.580
Where's the magic in that?

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:25.139
Zatanna, when did you...

00:10:25.139 --> 00:10:27.139
We need to talk, Plur. Alone.

00:10:27.139 --> 00:10:35.200
I hope it's okay that I borrow him for a bit.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.200
Lois, Zatana. Zatana. Zatanna.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.200
Zatana, Lois.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:42.090
Not exactly what I meant.

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:44.090
about being swept away.

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:56.500
I guess I shouldn't be surprised that you decided to follow in your father's footsteps.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:58.500
A lot can change in a year.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:03.100
Somehow, I don't think you detoured your roadshow to play catch-up.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:09.100
I found out my late great father got cocky and went on a cursing spray in his roaring 20s.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:16.799
I have been cleaning up his mess, rounding up all the things that he cursed.

00:11:16.799 --> 00:11:19.799
You think this stolen comic book was one of those items?

00:11:19.799 --> 00:11:21.799
It's not as crazy as it sounds.

00:11:21.799 --> 00:11:23.799
According to my dad's journal, our theme,

00:11:23.799 --> 00:11:26.799
is bound to be feeling the effects of true power,

00:11:26.799 --> 00:11:28.799
just like in the comic.

00:11:28.799 --> 00:11:30.799
I'm normally a solo act,

00:11:30.799 --> 00:11:33.799
but these things never seem to end well.

00:11:33.799 --> 00:11:38.799
And I can't think of anyone better to help me with this

00:11:38.799 --> 00:11:40.799
than you.

00:11:40.799 --> 00:11:45.509
Wait your car!

00:11:45.509 --> 00:11:49.299
Excuse me one moment.

00:11:49.299 --> 00:12:00.879
Lois, why you in the men's bathroom?

00:12:00.879 --> 00:12:04.879
You obviously haven't seen the line for the women's room.

00:12:04.879 --> 00:12:05.879
Lois.

00:12:05.879 --> 00:12:06.879
Just a minute.

00:12:06.879 --> 00:12:07.879
A minute.

00:12:07.879 --> 00:12:22.360
Stop gawking and prosper.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:23.360
That's what was in your back.

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:26.360
This Amazon Princess won't get nerdwalled again.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:32.360
Well, I still don't understand how this qualifies as Amazon, but whatever.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:35.360
So while I was waiting for you to drag your heels across the county line...

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:38.360
The story finally happened right under my nose.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:39.360
Someone stole...

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.360
The Rare Warrior Angel comic book.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.379
I know.

00:12:44.379 --> 00:12:48.379
My friend Zatanna told me she's into antiquities.

00:12:48.379 --> 00:12:50.379
There's a few leases that she wants me to help her track down.

00:12:50.379 --> 00:12:52.379
I'll bet you do.

00:12:52.379 --> 00:12:54.379
Louis, it's not like that.

00:12:54.379 --> 00:12:56.379
No, I get it.

00:12:56.379 --> 00:12:58.379
Do you mind if I get a picture with you?

00:12:58.379 --> 00:13:03.179
Make a picture?

00:13:03.179 --> 00:13:13.580
We'll cover more ground if we split it up anywhere, right?

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:17.299
The hell?

00:13:17.299 --> 00:13:18.299
Uh-huh.

00:13:18.299 --> 00:13:28.940
And you made sure that my decaf, Carmel Java chip white chocolate mocha,

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:29.940
has three shots in it, right?

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:30.940
Yeah.

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:31.940
Great.

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:32.940
And for you, sir.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:38.120
Uh, a glass of milk would be great.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.120
I'm... I mean coffee.

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:42.120
Dark, black.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:53.100
Please.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:54.100
Okay.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:58.100
Yeah, strong resolve.

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:02.100
So, if I'm gonna help you get acclimated, I just need to ask you...

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:04.100
You really know superheroes?

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:07.500
Yeah.

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:08.500
Now let's just focus on...

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:09.500
All of them.

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:12.500
Most of them, I guess.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:14.500
What?

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:18.500
You know actual superheroes and you couldn't sound more bored.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.500
That's... that's amazing is what it is.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.500
Well, it's a living.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:25.500
Can you at least tell me which heroes you know?

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:28.500
No, wait, don't. That would compromise their identities.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:30.500
I can't believe I ask that.

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:32.500
Let's just focus on what makes Steven Swift so super.

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:34.500
So were you exposed to media rock?

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:36.500
Or, uh, maybe you were actually born this way?

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.500
That would make you metahuman.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:43.649
Or maybe you're... from space.

00:14:43.649 --> 00:14:47.539
That last one was a joke.

00:14:47.539 --> 00:14:51.539
Kind of. Oh, God, you're not actually from space, are you?

00:14:51.539 --> 00:14:54.539
No. Just...

00:14:54.539 --> 00:14:58.740
Sorry. I'm an orphan.

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:02.740
And I got sent to Metropolis to live with my aunt when I was...

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:06.720
Little.

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:09.720
And then a couple weeks ago, I got caught in a...

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:12.720
in a chemical fire, and...

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:17.220
Well, here we are.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:18.220
It's common to the archetype.

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:19.220
Yeah.

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:21.220
I thought that was the expert.

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:29.159
I got to get home.

00:15:29.159 --> 00:15:31.159
And who's gonna stop me.

00:15:31.159 --> 00:15:35.720
Excuse me, Miss Sullivan.

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:43.980
Stop it!

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:45.980
You heard the man.

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:47.980
Leave him be.

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:49.980
What you're doing to this kid here isn't right.

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:52.980
And it isn't fair, and he shouldn't let you get away with it.

00:15:52.980 --> 00:15:53.980
Not ever.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:55.980
Mind your own business.

00:15:55.980 --> 00:16:05.509
I'll give you something to laugh about.

00:16:05.509 --> 00:16:11.340
Apologize!

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:29.019
Thanks, mister!

00:16:29.019 --> 00:16:36.929
Sorry, I just had to save the day.

00:16:36.929 --> 00:16:39.929
So, what's next?

00:16:39.929 --> 00:16:51.700
Sorry, my locator's spell wasn't more accurate.

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:54.700
Like I said, I need all the help I can get.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:59.549
We should be... close?

00:16:59.549 --> 00:17:03.549
I guess you can't expect magic to be an exact science.

00:17:03.549 --> 00:17:05.549
Was that a clever place?

00:17:05.549 --> 00:17:09.549
on words, wonderful wit and sparkling theatrics.

00:17:09.549 --> 00:17:11.549
Mr. Blur's really up to his game.

00:17:11.549 --> 00:17:31.910
Found it.

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:33.910
I always knew you're packing some heavy artillery

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:37.910
under that tie, but seeing through walls?

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:39.910
Oh, that's a showstopper.

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:41.910
All in day's work, I guess.

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.910
Wait.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:48.910
With powers like yours, how can you possibly say all in a day's work?

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:50.910
I don't really think about it.

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:53.910
Just being like this is almost like breathing now.

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:58.910
And with a gift like that, comes responsibilities.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:17:59.910
Exactly.

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:07.119
I've spent so much time trying to do what's right, then I guess I haven't had any time for anything but reality.

00:18:07.119 --> 00:18:13.119
And these people, out here with their capes, I don't know, they just don't get it.

00:18:13.119 --> 00:18:16.849
But...

00:18:16.849 --> 00:18:17.849
Right there with you.

00:18:17.849 --> 00:18:21.849
Magic, fantasy, it's all in today's work.

00:18:21.849 --> 00:18:23.849
Day in, day out.

00:18:23.849 --> 00:18:26.849
What I create is everyone else's fantasies is...

00:18:26.849 --> 00:18:29.849
become so normal.

00:18:29.849 --> 00:18:38.900
I suppose even the illusionist can become disillusioned.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:42.900
At least you have that fiery space trooper to Stargaze with at the end of the day.

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:47.880
Yeah, well...

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:52.880
At least on my last relationship, I'm afraid I'm keeping lowest at an arm's length.

00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:56.880
You're afraid that if you let that spark ignite, you're going to get burned again.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:19:00.859
Right now, everything's under control.

00:19:00.859 --> 00:19:05.339
Fantasy isn't about being in control.

00:19:05.339 --> 00:19:07.339
And fire...

00:19:07.339 --> 00:19:10.339
It doesn't always have to burn, you know.

00:19:10.339 --> 00:19:15.339
Maybe what you need is a tiny moment of true fantasy

00:19:15.339 --> 00:19:19.339
to remind you what sparks are all about.

00:19:19.339 --> 00:19:26.259
Dumetess.

00:19:26.259 --> 00:19:27.259
I'm good, thanks.

00:19:27.259 --> 00:19:28.259
No.

00:19:28.259 --> 00:19:31.859
No, you're not.

00:19:31.859 --> 00:19:39.619
Sparks lead to flames and fire is what keeps us alive.

00:19:39.619 --> 00:19:44.970
Now, Wolfet Etwa-Aq.

00:19:44.970 --> 00:20:09.680
I can't do this.

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:14.210
That's a shame.

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:20.440
I think we found a mouth more magical than mine.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:54.500
Hey, Oliver, what's up?

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:55.500
Me?

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:58.500
Just, uh, owed Lois some sharks tickets.

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:02.750
But you, buddy.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:05.750
